 put('formatting-slides.html','Format a presentation',intro('A good deck starts from the right template and is built around what your audience needs to take away.','presentations.html','Find presentation resources','Self-service guide')+steps([('Start from the right template','Use the '+link('standard-template.html','Standard SKAO template')+', or a '+link('partner-templates.html','partner template')+' for joint work, so the layouts, colours and type are already set.'),('Give each slide one job','Write a short heading that says the point of the slide, and use the supplied layouts so spacing and alignment stay consistent.'),('Let images and charts explain','Use them to make the point rather than decorate, and keep their sources and credits on the slide or in the notes.'),('Check facts and figures','Construction moves quickly, so check facts, dates and any adapted claims with the content owner. The '+link('low-slides.html','SKA-Low')+' and '+link('mid-slides.html','SKA-Mid')+' progress pages have the latest status.'),('Test it where you’ll present','Run the deck on the screen you’ll use and check text and charts read from the back of the room. Check contrast and alternative text, and caption any video.')]))
